WEBVTT

00:00:08.665 --> 00:00:09.905
It's headed for City Hall!

00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:13.025
-DASH: Mom needs help!
-(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

00:00:17.745 --> 00:00:19.945
They're out in public again!
This is our chance!

00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:22.145
Follow them, follow Frozone!

00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:32.665
(STRAINING)

00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:38.945
Bob!
Help me with the boiler!

00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:43.185
(GRUNTS)

00:00:55.505 --> 00:00:56.985
That should do it! (GASPS)

00:00:57.145 --> 00:00:58.985
What are you kids doing?
Get out of here!

00:00:59.145 --> 00:01:00.345
This thing's gonna blow!

00:01:00.505 --> 00:01:02.065
There's no time!

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.225
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:01:08.745 --> 00:01:10.145
(SIRENS WAILING)

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.945
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:15.865
We did it!

00:01:16.025 --> 00:01:17.385
-(GUNS COCKING)
-OFFICER: Freeze, Supers!

00:01:17.465 --> 00:01:19.745
Oh, what did we do?

00:01:21.105 --> 00:01:22.745
(PEOPLE EXCLAIMING)

00:01:23.785 --> 00:01:26.385
TOMMY: Excuse me, Mr. Zone?

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:31.345
FROZONE: Sorry, but I'm not
really supposed to be here.

00:01:31.505 --> 00:01:33.185
TOMMY: Which seems wrong...

00:01:33.345 --> 00:01:34.505
doesn't it?

00:01:34.665 --> 00:01:38.265
Perhaps you'd be interested in
changing that law?

00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:41.625
Superheroes including Frozone,

00:01:41.745 --> 00:01:43.345
Mr. Incredible,
and Elastigirl...

00:01:43.505 --> 00:01:45.585
caused further damage
to the city.

00:01:45.785 --> 00:01:47.825
The Underminer
remains at large.

00:01:47.985 --> 00:01:49.625
We didn't start this fight.

00:01:49.785 --> 00:01:50.825
Well, you didn't
finish it either!

00:01:50.905 --> 00:01:53.185
Did you stop the Underminer
from inflicting more damage?

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:54.385
No.

00:01:54.505 --> 00:01:55.785
Did you stop him
from robbing the banks?

00:01:55.945 --> 00:01:57.545
-No.
-Did you catch him?

00:01:57.705 --> 00:01:59.745
-No.
-The banks were insured.

00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:01.265
We have infrastructure
in place

00:02:01.345 --> 00:02:02.385
to deal with these matters.

00:02:02.545 --> 00:02:04.225
If you had simply
done nothing...

00:02:04.385 --> 00:02:05.785
everything would now be

00:02:05.865 --> 00:02:07.105
proceeding
in an orderly fashion.

00:02:07.345 --> 00:02:09.585
You'd have preferred
we do nothing?

00:02:09.745 --> 00:02:11.305
Without a doubt.

00:02:15.545 --> 00:02:16.945
You weren't much help.

00:02:17.105 --> 00:02:18.985
Do you want out of the hole?

00:02:19.145 --> 00:02:22.145
First you gotta
put down the shovel.

00:02:25.025 --> 00:02:27.025
Well, that went poorly.

00:02:27.905 --> 00:02:29.985
Dad, this is probably

00:02:30.065 --> 00:02:33.345
not the best time
to tell you about this...

00:02:33.545 --> 00:02:36.385
but something else
happened today with a kid...

00:02:37.305 --> 00:02:39.185
and my mask.

00:02:44.305 --> 00:02:45.985
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:02:52.665 --> 00:02:53.865
Oh, hey, Rick.

00:02:53.985 --> 00:02:56.585
Violet thinks a friend
of hers, a kid named Tony...

00:02:56.745 --> 00:02:59.505
might have seen her in the
outfit, without her mask.

00:02:59.665 --> 00:03:01.545
-Talkative type?
-Don't know.

00:03:01.705 --> 00:03:02.985
Last name is Rydinger.

00:03:03.145 --> 00:03:05.225
Tony Rydinger.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.985
I'll check it out.

00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:08.465
Bob, Helen...

00:03:08.625 --> 00:03:11.065
a word if you don't mind.

00:03:11.305 --> 00:03:13.945
Uh, the program's been
shut down.

00:03:14.105 --> 00:03:15.225
What?

00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:17.345
Politicians
don't understand people...

00:03:17.545 --> 00:03:20.665
who do good simply
because it's right.

00:03:20.825 --> 00:03:22.465
It makes 'em nervous.

00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:25.145
DICKER: They've been gunning
for Supers for years.

00:03:25.345 --> 00:03:27.465
Today was all they needed.

00:03:27.745 --> 00:03:29.425
Anyway...

00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:30.745
I'm done.

00:03:30.905 --> 00:03:33.025
I'm afraid two more weeks
in the motel

00:03:33.105 --> 00:03:34.385
is the best I can do for ya.

00:03:34.545 --> 00:03:35.585
It ain't much.

00:03:35.745 --> 00:03:36.785
You've done plenty, Rick.

00:03:36.945 --> 00:03:38.545
We won't forget.

00:03:38.705 --> 00:03:40.745
Well, it has been
a great honor

00:03:40.865 --> 00:03:42.185
working with you good people.

00:03:42.345 --> 00:03:44.665
Thanks for everything,
and good luck.

00:03:44.865 --> 00:03:47.145
Yeah. You, too.

00:03:57.865 --> 00:03:59.625
(JACK-JACK COOING)

00:04:01.465 --> 00:04:03.225
Did you wash your hands?

00:04:04.705 --> 00:04:07.025
-(WATER RUNNING)
-With soap?

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:10.625
VIOLET: Did you dry them?

00:04:14.585 --> 00:04:19.225
What? Is this all vegetables?
Who ordered all vegetables?

00:04:19.385 --> 00:04:21.105
I did. They're good
and you're going to have some.

00:04:21.185 --> 00:04:22.185
(GROANS)

00:04:22.465 --> 00:04:25.145
Are we going to talk about it?

00:04:25.225 --> 00:04:27.385
-What?
-The elephant in the room.

00:04:27.545 --> 00:04:29.825
-What elephant?
-I guess not then.

00:04:29.985 --> 00:04:30.985
You're referring to today.

00:04:31.065 --> 00:04:32.825
Yeah, what's the deal
with today?

00:04:32.985 --> 00:04:34.225
We all made mistakes.

00:04:34.385 --> 00:04:35.665
For example,

00:04:35.745 --> 00:04:37.265
you kids were supposed
to watch Jack-Jack.

00:04:37.425 --> 00:04:40.665
Babysitting, while you guys
did the important stuff.

00:04:40.745 --> 00:04:41.745
We talked about this.

00:04:41.825 --> 00:04:43.745
You're not old enough
to decide about these things.

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:44.985
We are old enough
to help out.

00:04:45.065 --> 00:04:46.065
Yeah!

00:04:46.145 --> 00:04:47.665
Isn't that what you tell us,
Dad?

00:04:47.825 --> 00:04:51.105
Yeah, well, "help out" can
mean many different things.

00:04:51.305 --> 00:04:52.865
But we're supposed to help,
if there's trouble.

00:04:52.945 --> 00:04:53.945
-Well, yeah, but...
-Aren't you

00:04:54.025 --> 00:04:55.905
-glad we helped today?
-Yeah, I know but...

00:04:56.065 --> 00:04:57.105
You said that you were
proud of us.

00:04:57.265 --> 00:04:58.905
Well, yeah, I was. Am!

00:04:59.105 --> 00:05:00.545
We wanna fight bad guys!

00:05:00.625 --> 00:05:02.865
-(BABBLING)
-No, you don't!

00:05:03.705 --> 00:05:05.585
You said things
were different now.

00:05:05.745 --> 00:05:07.945
And they were, on the island.

00:05:08.105 --> 00:05:09.585
But I didn't mean
that from now on...

00:05:09.745 --> 00:05:12.265
So now, we've gotta go back to
never using our powers.

00:05:12.425 --> 00:05:13.745
It defines who I am.

00:05:13.905 --> 00:05:15.425
We're not saying you have...

00:05:15.585 --> 00:05:17.465
-What?
-Someone on TV said it.

00:05:17.665 --> 00:05:19.065
Can we just eat?

00:05:19.225 --> 00:05:21.865
The dinner, while it's hot?

00:05:22.025 --> 00:05:23.545
Did we do something wrong?

00:05:23.705 --> 00:05:24.985
-Yes.
-BOB: No.

00:05:25.145 --> 00:05:27.425
We didn't do anything wrong.

00:05:27.585 --> 00:05:29.865
Superheroes are illegal.

00:05:29.945 --> 00:05:31.665
Whether it's fair or not,
that's the law.

00:05:31.825 --> 00:05:34.705
The law should be fair.
What are we teaching our kids?

00:05:34.865 --> 00:05:35.865
To respect the law!

00:05:35.945 --> 00:05:37.545
Even when the law
is disrespectful?

00:05:37.705 --> 00:05:40.265
If laws are unjust,
there are laws to change them!

00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:41.545
Otherwise, it's chaos!

00:05:41.705 --> 00:05:43.585
Which is exactly what we have!

00:05:49.745 --> 00:05:51.665
I just thought
it was kinda cool.

00:05:51.865 --> 00:05:55.545
-What was?
-Fighting crime as a family.

00:05:55.665 --> 00:05:58.465
(SIGHS) It was cool.

00:05:59.105 --> 00:06:01.785
But it's over.
The world is what it is.

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:03.945
We have to adapt.

00:06:04.105 --> 00:06:05.705
Are things bad?

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.345
Things are fine.

00:06:08.665 --> 00:06:09.785
May I be excused?

00:06:12.025 --> 00:06:13.425
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING ON TV)

00:06:13.985 --> 00:06:15.985
How much longer
in the motel, Dad?

00:06:16.985 --> 00:06:19.745
-Uh...
-Not much longer, honey.

